# Code owners — required reviewers for the files that hold the keys.
#
# This repository is PUBLIC. Anyone may fork it and open a pull request. GitHub
# already refuses to run a fork's workflow definitions with this repo's secrets,
# so a PR that edits .github/workflows/ cannot execute against them — but it
# CAN be merged, and after merging it runs with everything.
#
# These entries make that path require an explicit review from the owner.
# Effective only with branch protection on main requiring code-owner review;
# without it, CODEOWNERS requests a review and nothing enforces it. See the
# "Self-maintenance" section of README.md.

# Everything, by default.
*                       @mfala22ss

# The security-critical set, listed separately so the intent survives a future
# broadening of the rule above:
#
#   workflows        — hold secrets, and claude.yml grants an agent contents:write
#   CODEOWNERS       — anyone who can edit this file can remove every other rule
#   .env.example     — the documented shape of the credential set
#   lib/db.js        — the only module that constructs a service-role client
#   agents/retainer  — the sole defence against the disk-full outage of 2026-07-20
/.github/workflows/     @mfala22ss
/.github/CODEOWNERS     @mfala22ss
/.env.example           @mfala22ss
/worker/lib/db.js       @mfala22ss
/worker/agents/retainer.js @mfala22ss
